<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 2.98 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 2.98 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0840 to the dollar, up from 3.0860 on Tuesday and at 1.8080 to the mark, up from 1.8085, it said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.98 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Tuesay's 2.90 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
